>>important for survival that he simply cannot afford to give it away just 
>>to kill a priest by himself.
> 
> 
> I thought, 2 posts ago, you didn't care if the guaranteed altar was
> unattended or not?

So what?  When I talk about a guaranteed altar in the main dungeon 
(which would be the less attractive solution for me), then I can have a 
different view as to its being attended than when I am talking about 
*creating* one.  If it is just another guaranteed altar, and it happens 
to have a priest, I might even be glad (if the priest is aligned), 
because I can donate in addition without having to backtrack to mine town.

On the other hand, when we are talking about creating an altar, you 
would need a different, more difficult ritual to have one with a priest 
than one without, isn't that obvious?  So either there should be only 
the second possibility, or the ritual for having an altar with a priest 
should be available only to a high-level character.

> It's not hard - well, it is hard, but the whole game's hard - to get buff
> enough to tackle an aligned priest without an artifact weapon - not
> through toe-to-toe pounding, but through devious means. A character
> who can do this can easily survive without telepathy until it can be
> regained.

Once again, I am not talking about making the game harder or less hard. 
  I don't care.  In my opinion, the game is not hard for a well-spoiled 
player.  I want to make the game depend more on your skills and 
knowledge (i.e. also the degree of spoiledness :-) ) and less on the 
whims of the rng.  It is just a matter of taste.  I prefer playing chess 
to gambling.  In nethack, random events are inevitable.  But the ideal 
situation would be, if you could beat the game no matter how bad luck 
the rng produces for you, provided you play well enough...

